/-!
# BF–RF correspondence with constructed homogeneous realizations

Closed-isotropy admissibility constructs the initial simply connected group,
closed isotropy, quotient, normalized invariant metric, and fundamental fields.
An invariant Ricci-flow family then determines the normalized frame and bracket
flow. Their global targets are constructed coherently on the original quotient
carrier, with actual metric pullback and jointly smooth comparison maps.

The analytic flow remains an input; these statements do not assert Ricci-flow
PDE existence or maximal-time existence.

AI-assistance disclosure: generated by OpenAI Codex on 2026-10-27.
-/

